            "blocks": [
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 1,
                    "text": "jsonImport Module",
                    "anchor": "jsonimport-module"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "**Maturity: Production-ready format capability** when used through the shared governed import lifecycle. External source/transport maturity is evaluated separately."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "`jsonImport` provides JSON-specific import support for the `nData/nImport` capability. It registers `.json` files with the shared import engine, streams JSON arrays into model chunks, and sends those chunks into the import data handler selected by the import header."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Use this module for JSON parsing and chunking behavior. Shared import orchestration, tenant dispatch, diagnostics, run history, access policy, validation-only execution, rollback hooks, and remote-source governance belong to `nData/nImport/import`."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Capability",
                    "anchor": "capability"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "The module contributes:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "unordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "`data.fileTypeProcess.json = 'jsonFileDataInitializerPipeline'`;",
                        "`jsonFileDataInitializerPipeline`;",
                        "`DefaultJsonFileDataProcessService`."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "JSON input is expected to be an array stream compatible with `stream-json/streamers/StreamArray`. Each array value becomes a model record."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Runtime Flow",
                    "anchor": "runtime-flow"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "ordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "The shared import module resolves a `.json` file to `jsonFileDataInitializerPipeline`.",
                        "`validateRequest` confirms `request.files` is an array and `request.outputPath` is present.",
                        "`processDataChunk` delegates to `handleFiles`.",
                        "Each JSON file is read as a stream.",
                        "`StreamArray` emits one array element at a time.",
                        "Records are accumulated until `data.readBufferSize` is exceeded.",
                        "Each chunk is assigned to `request.models`.",
                        "Import diagnostics increment `recordsRead` when diagnostics are active.",
                        "`request.outputPath.version` is set from file index and chunk version.",
                        "The import header's `options.dataHandler` pipeline processes the chunk."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Configuration",
                    "anchor": "configuration"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Default configuration:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "code",
                    "language": "js",
                    "text": "module.exports = {\n    data: {\n        fileTypeProcess: {\n            json: 'jsonFileDataInitializerPipeline'\n        }\n    }\n};"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Chunk size is controlled by the shared `data.readBufferSize` property owned by the import lifecycle configuration."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Extension Path",
                    "anchor": "extension-path"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Projects may customize JSON import by:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "unordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "contributing import headers and data handlers for JSON payloads;",
                        "overriding `DefaultJsonFileDataProcessService` in a later active module;",
                        "adding schema validation, validators, interceptors, or transformation processors;",
                        "adding project-specific tests for JSON payload shape and tenant behavior."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Keep cross-format import rules in the shared import module. JSON-specific behavior should stay in this module or in a later project override."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Tests",
                    "anchor": "tests"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Current module coverage includes common and environment-local smoke tests. Changes to parsing or chunking should add focused tests for:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "unordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "missing files and missing output path;",
                        "non-array request file input;",
                        "JSON array streaming;",
                        "chunking by `data.readBufferSize`;",
                        "diagnostics `recordsRead` increments;",
                        "`request.outputPath.version` behavior;",
                        "malformed JSON failure behavior;",
                        "project override behavior."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Run:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "code",
                    "language": "bash",
                    "text": "npm run test:import\nnpm run test:basic\nnpm run quality:docs"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "What To Avoid",
                    "anchor": "what-to-avoid"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Avoid:"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "unordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "assuming JSON payloads are trusted because they are structured;",
                        "bypassing schema and access-policy validation;",
                        "loading very large JSON files fully into memory when streaming is required;",
                        "changing chunk behavior without tests;",
                        "putting project-specific transformation in the framework parser;",
                        "editing generated import artifacts manually."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Operations And Boundaries",
                    "anchor": "operations-and-boundaries"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "paragraph",
                    "text": "Define encoding, size, record-count, malformed-input, batching, and partial-failure behavior for production workloads."
                },
                {
                    "kind": "heading",
                    "level": 2,
                    "text": "Continue",
                    "anchor": "continue"
                },
                {
                    "kind": "unordered-list",
                    "items": [
                        "Import family: [nImport](../README.md)",
                        "Shared engine: [import](../import/README.md)",
                        "Data processing: [dataCore](../../dataCore/README.md)",
                        "Public data guide: [How To Work With Data](../../../../gDocs/data/how-to-work-with-data.md)"
                    ]
                }
            ],
